{"content":{"result":[{"rank_order":1,"title":"AWS Elemental MediaTailor now offers Yield Optimization to automatically fill ad breaks with Amazon Ads demand - AWS","context":"AWS Elemental MediaTailor has introduced a new feature called Yield Optimization, which automatically monetizes unused ad inventory during server-side ad insertion (SSAI) for livestreams. This capability is exclusive to publishers in the Amazon Publisher Services (APS) Streaming TV program and comes at no additional cost. Yield optimization turns unfilled ad breaks into monetized impressions, enabling publishers to maximize their revenue without requiring any extra infrastructure or client-side changes.\n\nThe feature is designed for large-scale live events, ensuring low latency and fast response times during peak viewership. Ads are stitched directly into the stream, ensuring seamless playback on every device. Publishers have control over which ads run in their streams by setting their own price floors and category rules.\n\nYield optimization is available in all AWS Regions where MediaTailor is available, including US East (Ohio), US East (N. Virginia), US West (Oregon), Africa (Cape Town), Asia Pacific (Hyderabad, Malaysia, Melbourne, Mumbai, Osaka, Seoul, Singapore, Sydney, Tokyo), Canada (Central), Europe (Frankfurt, Ireland, London, Paris, Stockholm), Middle East (UAE), and South America (São Paulo). Publishers can monitor ad fill rate improvements using MediaTailor metrics in Amazon CloudWatch and track revenue and earnings through the APS Publisher portal","url":"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/whats-new/2026/09/mediatailor-yield-optimization/"},{"rank_order":2,"title":"AWS Elemental MediaTailor Monetization Functions adds ad response hooks - AWS","context":"AWS Elemental MediaTailor, a video service offered by Amazon Web Services (AWS), has introduced two new monetization functions: post ad decision server (ADS) response and pre manifest insertion. MediaTailor personalizes and inserts ads into live and on-demand streams, and these functions allow customers to run custom logic at defined points in an ad-personalized playback session. The post ADS response hook runs after MediaTailor parses an ADS response and resolves all VAST wrappers, enabling customers to call a secondary ad source when the primary one returns insufficient demand, remove disallowed ads based on content or brand policies, and add house ads or promotions from their marketing systems. The pre manifest insertion hook runs at the last point before MediaTailor returns the ad pod to the viewer, allowing customers to make a final check on what is about to play and insert personalized slates when necessary. Both hooks are fail-open, meaning they discard the function output and continue with default ad insertion on a timeout, expression error, or resource limit. These hooks are available in all AWS Regions where MediaTailor is available. To learn more, customers can refer to the Monetization Functions section in the AWS Elemental MediaTailor User Guide and the MediaTailor pricing page. To get started, they should sign in to the AWS Elemental MediaTailor console. MediaTailor is available in all AWS Regions where it is offered. For a complete list, customers can check the AWS Regional Services List","url":"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/whats-new/2026/09/aws-elemental-mediatailor-functions-ad-response-hooks/"},{"rank_order":3,"title":"AWS Elemental MediaTailor adds configurable ad timeout and concurrency controls for improved ad fill and faster startup - AWS","context":"AWS Elemental MediaTailor, a service offered by Amazon Web Services (AWS), has introduced new features that allow users to configure ad decision server (ADS) timeouts and concurrency controls. Previously, these settings required contacting AWS Support for modifications. The new settings include individual HTTP ad request timeouts, total ad personalization time budgets for live, VOD, and live ad prefetch, and the ability to enable parallel ADS requests. These adjustments enable users to optimize ad delivery performance for their specific workflows. For instance, increasing the personalization time budget for live events can enhance ad fill rates, while enabling parallel ADS requests in VOD workflows can decrease overall response time for faster video startup. Additionally, new prefetch-specific timeout settings offer more granularity for livestream ad retrieval. Users can configure these settings through the AWS Elemental MediaTailor console, AWS CLI, or AWS SDKs using the new AdsPersonalizationTimeouts and AdsPersonalizationConcurrency parameters on playback configurations. This feature is accessible in all AWS Regions where AWS Elemental MediaTailor is available. For more information on configuring ADS request timeouts, personalization time budgets, and concurrency, refer to the Advanced settings section in the AWS Elemental MediaTailor User Guide","url":"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/whats-new/2026/07/mediatail-configurable-ad-timeout-and-concurrency/"},{"rank_order":4,"title":"testing-mwaa-workflow","skill_description":"Tests Amazon MWAA workflow execution end-to-end: trigger a run and monitor it to completion for Provisioned (Python DAG, via Airflow REST API) and Serverless (YAML workflow, via StartWorkflowRun). Verifies the artifact is deployed and parse-ready, triggers with confirmation, polls to terminal state, and on failure delegates diagnosis to debugging-mwaa-workflow and artifact/redeploy fixes to authoring-mwaa-workflow, then retests up to a capped number of attempts. Triggers on: test my DAG, test my workflow, run my DAG, trigger a test run, does my DAG work, smoke-test the pipeline, verify my workflow runs, execute my DAG to check it. Not applicable to writing or deploying a new workflow (handled by authoring-mwaa-workflow), or for diagnosing why a run failed or root-causing an error (handled by debugging-mwaa-workflow).\n\n\nServices: mwaa\nTasks: test\nPersona: data-engineer\nWorkload: analytics, orchestration\n*","skill_name":"testing-mwaa-workflow"},{"rank_order":5,"title":"aws-ai-ml","skill_description":"Selects, deploys, and customizes AI models on Amazon SageMaker. Training or Processing jobs, fine-tuning (SFT/DPO/RLVR/RLAIF), model selection, dataset preparation, evaluation, SageMaker or Bedrock deployment, inference optimization and endpoint diagnostics. Covers the full lifecycle from planning through production. Use when fine-tuning models on SageMaker, choosing which base model to customize, fine-tune, or deploy from SageMaker JumpStart or Hub, SageMakerPublicHub, or the SageMaker public model catalog, transforming or validating training data, evaluating model quality, deploying or optimizing endpoints, configuring IAM/S3 for training, or managing SageMaker Managed MLflow. Use for endpoint health, failures, latency, logs, metrics, errors. Covers Serverless Model Customization, Nova and OSS deployment paths, and PySDK v3. NOT for Ground Truth labeling, Feature Store, or general-purpose AWS infrastructure.\n\nServices: sagemaker, s3, iam, bedrock\nTasks: build, deploy, debug, optimize\nPersona: developer, data-scientist\nWorkload: ai-ml\n*","skill_name":"aws-ai-ml"}]}}"}]}], "label": "Look up AWS MediaTailor docs on PersonalizationThresholdSeconds behavior."}
